11900	{"artifactId":"LLD-cb09a32ccdc4ed2b-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-cb09a32ccdc4ed2b-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T17:09:30.677Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Epic's own records (DEF, HLD, epic-level amendments, SPEC) are already on the Epic item in the snapshot, so ac1 can be met from the snapshot alone with no daemon change.","evidence":"src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts:223-230 builds the epic draft with `evidenceArtifactIds: epicLevel.map(r => r.artifactId)`; groupKeyOf (graph.ts:42-50) puts every record with no story id under the epic-level key `${hash}|`; SPECs are appended at graph.ts:565 (`item.evidenceArtifactIds.push(r.artifactId)`). src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts:102-110 gives every evidence entry mdPath/openWith/approval/review, which is what ac1 (approval and review state) and ac2 (review pane vs read-only) need. The table will also list any other epic-level record (e.g. a pending EXT), which is consistent with 'the Epic's records'. [files: src/workflow/delivery/graph.ts, src/workflow/delivery/snapshot.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the details memory has no selection on an Epic's board, so none of the Epic's records can be opened.","evidence":"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts:118-121: `return screen.kind === 'item' ? screen.itemId : null;` and board-host.ts:536 `memory.kept(shown, currentItemId(next.selection));`. details-memory.ts:164 `const item = itemId === selected ? itemOf(itemId) : undefined;` refuses anything that is not the selection. The 'epic' case of screenBody (board-state.ts:387-393) never calls detailsOf. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"renderStages today draws the totals line first and returns early on the no-matches panel, so the records box must be appended before both to survive an empty filter result.","evidence":"board-host.ts:186: `function renderStages(b){renderTotals(b.totalsLabel,b.showAll);if(b.emptyPanel!==null){renderPanel(bodyEl,b.emptyPanel);return;}`. bodyEl is cleared before the switch at board-host.ts:296-297, so appending first puts the box at the top of the body. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"recordOwnerId, EpicRecordsView and StagesBody.epicRecords do not exist yet.","evidence":"Grep for `currentItemId|recordOwnerId|epicRecords` over vscode-plugin returns only currentItemId (board-state.ts:118, board-host.ts:41 and 536). StagesBody (board-protocol.ts:229-240) has kind, epic, totalsLabel, showAll, sections, fold, emptyPanel only. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused pieces have the stated shape: memory.model builds details for any item (an Epic included) and attaches the opened record only for the memory's selection; detailsOf is null only when the item is not in the snapshot; recordsTable reads only d.evidence and d.itemId.","evidence":"details-memory.ts:136-142: `const record = snap === snapshot && itemId === selected ? opened : null; return buildItemDetails(snap, itemId, plan, record, deps.labels);`. board-details.ts:200-201 returns null only when `byId.get(itemId)` is undefined, and line 215 maps `item.evidence.map(e => evidenceRow(e, labels))` with no kind check. board-host.ts:534 passes `id => (shown === null ? null : memory.model(shown, id))`. recordsTable (board-host.ts:246-252) touches only `d.evidence` and `d.itemId`. OpenedRecord is exported from board-details.ts:37 and EvidenceRowView from board-protocol.ts:159. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-details.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts]","action":"None. Note for the build: apply() derives the messages before memory.kept (board-host.ts:534-536), so the first render of an Epic's board has no opened record, which is correct; the record appears on the rerender after readRecord, as for a Story.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"memory.kept(currentItemId(...)) is the single call site to change in the host, and currentItemId 'stays as it is for its other users'.","evidence":"The single-call-site part is true: the only use of currentItemId outside its definition is board-host.ts:536 (plus its import at line 41). The 'other users' wording is inaccurate: a grep over vscode-plugin finds no other user, in source or tests, so after the change currentItemId is an unused export and the import at board-host.ts:41 becomes unused. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts]","action":"In the build, drop the unused import in board-host.ts and either remove currentItemId or define recordOwnerId in terms of it; also update the host's header comment (board-host.ts:30-33, 'null on any other screen') and the details-memory header, which say the selection is a story or issue.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The inventory for the required field StagesBody.epicRecords is complete: one constructor (buildBoardViewModel) plus the spread in the 'epic' case.","evidence":"Grep for `kind: 'stages'` finds one object literal, board-model.ts:367. board-state.ts:392 spreads it (`{ ...body, epic: epicRowOf(...) }`). The tests import StagesBody as a type only (board-state.test.ts:51, board-host.test.ts:92, board-model.test.ts:18, board-views.test.ts:27) and build none by hand; no test deep-compares a whole StagesBody. The webview reads it in renderStages only (board-host.ts:186, 295). [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-model.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Selecting an Epic in the memory reads no plan.","evidence":"details-memory.ts:51-52: `if (item === undefined || item.kind !== 'story') return null;` and kept() at 157-158 returns when `planId === null`; model() at 137-138 gives `{ state: 'none' }` for a null planId. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change is a host-to-webview message shape only: nothing is stored, the daemon contract is untouched, and the host and webview cannot be at different versions.","evidence":"The webview script is a string constant in the host module (board-host.ts:87 `export const BOARD_WEBVIEW_SCRIPT`) set into the panel by renderBoardDocument (board-host.ts:475-498, 741), so both ends ship in one build. The down-message is rebuilt from state on every apply (board-host.ts:532-539) and never persisted; the webview keeps only density in vs.setState (board-host.ts:319-321). The evidence rows come from fields the snapshot already carries (delivery types.ts:274-283). [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-host.ts, src/workflow/delivery/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The three open failures are detected and handled by existing code unchanged: a record that is not the selection's is refused and logged; with no review pane a reviewable record is read and shown read-only; a failed read becomes 'Could not read <id>: <message>'.","evidence":"details-memory.ts:164-169 (`log.warn('delivery board: ignored a request to open a record that is not the selected item\\'s evidence'); return;`), 172 (`entry.openWith === 'review-view' && entry.mdPath !== null && deps.reviewPane !== undefined` else falls to readRecord), 94-98 (a throw becomes a typed read-failed result) and 127-129 (`text = `Could not read ${artifactId}: ${result.failure.message}``). None of these branches on the item's kind, so they apply to an Epic selection as written. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The stated edge behaviour is what the memory does: a selection or snapshot change drops the opened record and any read in flight; opening another record in the review pane leaves the read-only record shown; changing the search or filter on the Epic's board keeps it.","evidence":"details-memory.ts:146-156: a new snapshot or `selectedItemId !== selected` sets `opened = null; epoch++`. Line 123 drops a late answer (`madeAt !== epoch`). Lines 171-175: the review-pane branch bumps epoch and returns without clearing `opened`. set-search/set-attention keep the same trail entry and epic id (board-state.ts:208-213), so recordOwnerId is unchanged and kept() clears nothing. A removed Epic cuts the trail (board-state.ts:136, 147-154), which changes the selection. [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/details-memory.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/board-state.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a named test that the existing test tooling can carry: the webview harness and the fixtures exist and can build an Epic with evidence.","evidence":"vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/ contains board-webview-harness.ts, board-fixtures.ts, board-state.test.ts, details-memory.test.ts and board-host.test.ts. board-fixtures.ts:25-29 `item(spec)` accepts any kind and evidence, and :54-56 `evidence(artifactId, kind, over)` defaults to `mdPath: null, openWith: 'evidence-read'` with overrides for a review-view record; largeSnapshot already builds `kind: 'epic'` items (:78). The mapping table covers ac1 (state + webview), ac2 (record owner + memory + host) and ac3 (unchanged-screens test + whole suite). [files: vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-fixtures.ts, vscode-plugin/src/delivery/__tests__/board-webview-harness.ts]","action":"None. For ac3, make the 'built exactly as before' test compare a Story's body and a list screen's body field by field (a list StagesBody now differs only by epicRecords: null), since the whole-suite check alone would not catch a new regression on the issue screen.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":12,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-13T17:09:30.677Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
